register_gate "tests/test_ci_script_contract.py" "CI SCRIPT CONTRACT GATE: PASS" "CI script contract graph" "GitHub Actions workflow run commands that explicitly invoke package-manager scripts now couple to the package.json script declaration through a content-free ci_script contract key. This closes the merge-gate blind spot where a PR edits package.json scripts and another edits the workflow that runs them, with no import or call edge between the files. Precision: definitions come only from package.json scripts; references come only from .github/workflows run entries; working-directory or cd resolves monorepo scripts uniquely, while a same-name call with no package context retains every candidate alters/queries edge with reference_status=ambiguous so effective adjacency excludes it without losing evidence; comments, non-run prose, and non-workflow yaml do not couple. Content-free: script names, package dirs, paths, and edge kinds only, never script bodies or workflow comments." "package.json scripts and GitHub Actions run commands are linked through a bounded, explicit ci_script contract; ambiguous monorepo script references remain durable evidence but never enter effective adjacency; prose/comment mentions stay silent; script bodies and workflow comments never enter the graph" 20
